<sect1 id="chapter2_1autotoc_md80_1s1"><sect2 id="chapter2_1autotoc_md80">
<title>Edge semantics</title><para>An empty formula with zero clauses is SAT by convention but still parsed as a valid problem. An empty clause denotes UNSAT structure and should be preserved as an empty clause entry. Literal sign encodes polarity; absolute value encodes variable index.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".text"><codeline><highlight class="normal">sattyre::SATProblem<sp/>p;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">p.variable_count<sp/>=<sp/>2;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">p.clauses<sp/>=<sp/>{<sp/>{1},<sp/>{-1,<sp/>2}<sp/>};</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<sect3 id="chapter2_1autotoc_md81">
